<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A boat is steered on a course of <m>{270}^\circ</m> at <m>{7}</m> knots through the water. A current flows towards <m>{180}^\circ</m> at <m>{3}</m> knots.</p><p>(a) Find the ground speed, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/> knots  </p><p>(b) Find the drift angle, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/> <m>^\circ</m>  </p><p>(c) Find the track, as a bearing correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p><fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/> <m>^\circ</m>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The course is where the boat points; the track is where it goes. Draw the course arrow (<m>{7}</m> knots towards <m>{270}^\circ</m>), then the current arrow from its tip (<m>{3}</m> knots towards <m>{180}^\circ</m>). The current is at right angles to the course, so the triangle is right-angled and the track arrow is its hypotenuse.</p><p>(a) Ground speed <m>= \sqrt{ {7}^2 + {3}^2} = {7.616} \approx {7.6}</m> knots.</p><p>(b) <m>\tan d = \dfrac{ {3} }{ {7} }</m>, so <m>d = {23.199}^\circ \approx {23.2}^\circ</m>.</p><p>(c) The current pushes the boat anticlockwise of its course, so the track is <m>{270}^\circ - {23.2}^\circ = {246.8}^\circ</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>7.61577310586</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>23.1985905136</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>246.801409486</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>